### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### e-car.eth — OEM endpoint collection
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Works with VS Code REST Client and JetBrains HTTP Client.
### Import into Postman via: File → Import → paste this file.
###
### Switch baseUrl between local + Railway by commenting/uncommenting below.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@baseUrl   = http://localhost:3001
# @baseUrl   = https://earnest-harmony-e-car.up.railway.app

@apiKey       = test-api-key
@adminSecret  = test-admin-secret
@brand        = tesla
@vehicleId    = 1
@oemWallet    = 0x1111111111111111111111111111111111111111
@buyerWallet  = 0x2222222222222222222222222222222222222222

### ─── 0. Health ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### ─── 1. Auth ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### List tiers (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/tiers

### Mint an API key (admin only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/keys
x-admin-secret: {{adminSecret}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "oem-tesla-pilot",
  "tier":  "oem"
}

### Get info for current key
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/keys/info
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### Revoke current key
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/auth/keys
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### ─── 2. Brand namespace ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/brands/{{brand}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/brands/{{brand}}/claim
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "signerAddress": "{{oemWallet}}"
}

### ─── 3. Vehicles ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vehicles/{{vehicleId}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vehicles
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "vin":                "5YJSA1H21FFP00001",
  "manufacturer":       "Tesla",
  "model":              "Model 3",
  "year":               2024,
  "batteryCapacityKwh": 82
}

### ─── 4. Batch preauthorize (the OEM 100K path) ──────────────────────────
### Submit a list of VINs. Returns batchId + merkleRoot.
### Use overrides[] to make specific VINs transferable while others are soulbound.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vehicles/batch/preauthorize
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "vins": [
    "OEM-QS-0001", "OEM-QS-0002", "OEM-QS-0003", "OEM-QS-0004",
    "OEM-QS-0005", "OEM-QS-0006", "OEM-QS-0007", "OEM-QS-0008"
  ],
  "manufacturer":       "Tesla",
  "model":              "Model 3",
  "year":               2026,
  "batteryCapacityKwh": 82,
  "soulbound":          true,
  "overrides": [
    { "vin": "OEM-QS-0003", "soulbound": false }
  ]
}

### Copy the `batchId` from above into the variable below before running the next 3 requests.
@batchId = paste-batchId-here

### Batch summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vehicles/batch/{{batchId}}
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### Single Merkle proof (public — used at claim time by the vehicle owner)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vehicles/batch/{{batchId}}/proof/OEM-QS-0001

### Paginated proofs (private — OEM batch fetch)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vehicles/batch/{{batchId}}/proofs?limit=100&offset=0
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### Bulk-transfer calldata (transferable NFTs only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vehicles/batch/{{batchId}}/transfer
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "from": "{{oemWallet}}",
  "transfers": [
    { "tokenId": "1", "to": "{{buyerWallet}}" },
    { "tokenId": "2", "to": "{{buyerWallet}}" }
  ]
}

### ─── 5. Battery passport ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/battery/{{vehicleId}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/battery/{{vehicleId}}/history

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/battery/{{vehicleId}}/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "leaf":  "0xdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeef",
  "proof": ["0xcafebabecafebabecafebabecafebabecafebabecafebabecafebabecafebabe"]
}

### ─── 6. Charging ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/charging/stations

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/charging/stations
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stationId":       "STATION-LA-001",
  "brand":           "{{brand}}",
  "pricePerKwh":     250000000000000,
  "operatorAddress": "{{oemWallet}}"
}

### Initiate a charging session (creates escrow)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/charging/sessions
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stationNodeId": "0x16ee195ce43464aa0159cc05a804b668373b135970534f28ae30daddc0c586c2",
  "vehicleId":     "{{vehicleId}}",
  "estimatedKwh":  30,
  "token":         "USDC"
}

### Finalize a session
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/charging/sessions/sess_1/finalize
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "escrowId":  "1",
  "actualKwh": 28.5
}

### ─── 7. Fleet ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/fleet
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name":            "Hertz NYC",
  "operatorAddress": "{{oemWallet}}",
  "vehicles":        ["1", "2"]
}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/fleet/abc/payments?period=30d
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### ─── 8. Carbon credits ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/carbon/{{vehicleId}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/carbon/{{vehicleId}}/mint
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "verifiedMileage": 1250,
  "odometerProof":   "0xproof..."
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/carbon/{{vehicleId}}/retire
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount":      5,
  "reason":      "ESG Q1 2026 — corporate ESG report",
  "beneficiary": "{{oemWallet}}"
}

### ─── 9. Voice + Ramp ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/voice/intent
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "utterance":  "Charge my car to 80% and pay with USDC",
  "vehicleId":  "{{vehicleId}}"
}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ramp/providers

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ramp/initiate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount":         100,
  "currency":       "USDC",
  "provider":       "moonpay",
  "walletAddress":  "{{oemWallet}}"
}

### ─── 10. Merkle utilities ───────────────────────────────────────────────
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/merkle/generate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "leaves": ["alpha", "bravo", "charlie", "delta"]
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/merkle/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "root":  "0xroot...",
  "proof": ["0x..."],
  "leaf":  "0xleaf..."
}
